-- =====================================================================
-- LLC — seed: General English Placement Assessment — Set 1
-- 50 grammar questions + 6 reading sections (30 questions), from the reference platform.
-- Run once in Supabase → SQL Editor AFTER 015. It does nothing if a test with this title exists.
-- The test is created approved but NOT active: open it from Placement Tests when you are ready.
-- =====================================================================
do $$
declare tid bigint; sid bigint; gid bigint;
begin
  if exists (select 1 from public.placement_tests where title = 'General English Placement Assessment — Set 1') then return; end if;
  values ('General English Placement Assessment — Set 1', $q$A short assessment designed to evaluate your current English proficiency and place you in the most suitable course level, ensuring you start learning at the level that best matches your skills.$q$, 60, false, 'language', 'both', 5, 'approved') returning id into tid;

How are you? I'm writing to tell you about my weekend plans. On Saturday morning, I'm going to the market with my mum to buy some fruit and vegetables. In the afternoon, my friends and I are going to watch a movie at the new cinema in town — it's the one with the big red sign near the bus station. On Sunday, I don't have any plans yet, but I might go swimming if the weather is nice. I hope to see you soon!

Love,
Maria$q$, 1) returning id into gid;

As you know, the second floor will be closed for refurbishment starting next Monday. During this period, staff who normally work on that floor will be temporarily relocated to the third floor. Please note that meeting rooms B and C will be unavailable throughout the two-week refurbishment, so any meetings currently booked in these rooms should be rescheduled or moved to another room. We apologise for any inconvenience this may cause and will keep you updated on our progress. If you have any questions, please contact facilities management directly rather than replying to this email, as it is sent from an unmonitored address.$q$, 1) returning id into gid;
end $$;
